 "narrative": "All estimates are signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive signed values support the claimed direction. The MSI-high context tests are decisive in the favorable direction. H117, MSI-high among TP53-loss-free and KEAP1-loss-free cells, gives signed estimate +0.766 with lower bound +0.667 and exposed n=81. H118, MSI-high in a clean background free of TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, and SMARCA4-loss, gives +0.745 with lower bound +0.666 and exposed n=62. H119, MSI-high within adenocarcinoma, gives +0.742 with lower bound +0.605 and exposed n=93. All three exceed the 0.15 composite-unit threshold, showing that the MSI-high association is not simply an artifact of the dominant TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4 co-alteration architecture and is also present in the majority subtype. I accept all three and keep them active as contingency claims while awaiting independent validation of the broader MSI-high claim H106. H106 is now the most valuable validation target because it is the only major accepted architecture component without independent validation; I request H106 validation. H120 refines EGFR amplification to TP53-loss-free cells and gives +0.074 with lower bound -0.026 and upper +0.173. It fails the threshold, does not clear acceptance, and provides no reason to continue EGFR follow-up; I leave H120 unresolved but closed, and close H58 investigation without changing its unresolved status. H121 tests whether SMARCA4-loss is stronger in adenocarcinoma than complement. The signed interaction estimate is -0.211 with interval [-0.359, -0.063], entirely opposite the claimed negative direction; if reversed, the bound nearest zero is only about +0.063, below threshold. I reject and close H121. H36, TP53-loss by adenocarcinoma interaction, gives -0.033 with interval reaching +0.184; the estimate is opposite and the interval is not adequate for acceptance, so it remains unresolved but is closed. H37, KEAP1-loss by adenocarcinoma interaction, gives -0.063 with favorable upper bound +0.076, well below threshold, so reject and close. The high-aneuploidy interactions are not modifier evidence: H122 gives +0.070 with interval [-0.150, +0.290], and H123 gives +0.021 with interval [-0.142, +0.183]; both fail threshold and are closed unresolved. H124, sex male versus female, gives signed -0.074 with interval [-0.138, -0.010], entirely opposite the claimed positive direction and well below threshold, so reject and close. H29, KEAP1-loss by research_signature_b interaction, gives +0.091 with interval [-0.039, +0.222]; it is not supported as a threshold interaction and is closed unresolved. H77, SMARCA4-loss among adults, gives +0.827 with lower +0.750 and exposed n=308, a large robust replication of the accepted SMARCA4-loss negative-dependency association; I accept and close it. I also close investigation of stale near-threshold or duplicated threads without changing their scientific statuses: H92 CDKN2A overall remains unresolved but closed because its TP53-loss-free context test failed; H20 and H65 remain unresolved but closed because the TP53/KEAP1 interaction has lower bounds near zero and no current path to acceptance without a better validation target; H107 remains accepted but closed as a PTEN context overlapping the validated H80 result. These conclusions remain observational associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable biological claims.",
 "research_notes": "Iteration 8 appraise: MSI-high is strongly supported in discovery contexts. H117, H118, and H119 all pass threshold and establish that MSI-high is not reducible to TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4 co-alteration and is present in adenocarcinoma. I requested independent validation for overall H106. If H106 validation clears threshold, MSI-high becomes a validated main supplied-dataset association and its investigation can be closed. If H106 validation fails, retain H117/H118 as conditional clean-background MSI associations and consider validation of the clean-background claim H118 rather than the overall claim. EGFR is closed: overall H58 remains unresolved, and TP53-loss-free refinement H120 failed to support follow-up. CDKN2A is closed after H109 and H92 did not clear threshold. Demographic and modifier screening mostly closes: sex H124 rejected; lineage/aneuploidy/signature_b/hypoxia interactions either rejected or unresolved closed. Adult SMARCA4 H77 accepted. Stale interactions H20/H65 and duplicate PTEN context H107 closed without changing status. Established architecture: TP53-loss positive/less-negative, KEAP1-loss positive/less-negative, and SMARCA4-loss negative/more-negative, all independently validated; PTEN-loss negative conditional on TP53-loss-free, validated; MSI-high negative pending H106 validation. All claims remain supplied-dataset observational associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
